WHAT
    Four changes to Slate's CMake so it configures against a Qt that has no
    qttools, no QtTest, and from a source tarball rather than a git checkout.

WHY
    Each is a hard configure error, not a warning:

    1. lib/CMakeLists.txt ends with
           else()
               message(FATAL_ERROR "Can not find .git repo")
           endif()
       so Slate cannot be built from a release tarball at all. This port
       fetches the pinned tarball on purpose -- the house rule is that build.sh
       fetches upstream and git never carries it. BUILD_VERSION is now an input
       the packager can supply (node/CMakeLists.txt passes the short commit),
       and it still comes from git when there is a git. It only ever reaches
       the About box.

    2. qt_add_translations() is called unconditionally, but the command only
       exists when Qt6LinguistTools was found -- and the find_package for it at
       the top of the file is deliberately not REQUIRED. On a Qt built without
       qttools (there is no wasm qttools here, and lrelease would be a host
       tool anyway) CMake dies with "Unknown CMake command". Guarded on the
       lrelease target, which is what the command actually needs.

    3. set_property(DIRECTORY tests ...) runs even when ENABLE_TESTING is OFF,
       and CMake errors out on a directory it was never given. The cross qtbase
       has FEATURE_testlib=OFF (QTestLib wants threads and a process launcher),
       so ENABLE_TESTING must be OFF here.

    4. -Weverything on clang. wasi-sdk 34's clang reports itself as Clang 23 and
       -Weverything emits tens of thousands of diagnostics for a Qt/QML
       codebase -- including -Wc++98-compat on a C++17 project -- which buries
       the real ones. Narrowed to -Wall -Wextra.

    1-3 are portable improvements that would help anyone packaging Slate;
    4 is a local preference and should not be sent upstream as-is.

UPSTREAM
    Worth offering: 1 (build from tarball), 2 and 3 (configure without
    qttools/QtTest). Not offered: 4.

CLASSIFICATION
    as-is -- no behaviour of the running program changes. The About box shows
    the pinned short commit instead of a live `git rev-parse`.
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@
 
 target_compile_options(projectWarning INTERFACE
     $<$<CXX_COMPILER_ID:GNU>:$<BUILD_INTERFACE:-Wall;-Wextra;-Wpedantic>>
-    $<$<CXX_COMPILER_ID:Clang>:$<BUILD_INTERFACE:-Weverything;-Wpedantic>>
+    $<$<CXX_COMPILER_ID:Clang>:$<BUILD_INTERFACE:-Wall;-Wextra>>
     $<$<CXX_COMPILER_ID:MSVC>:/W0>
 )
 
@@ -33,12 +33,14 @@
 add_subdirectory(lib)
 add_subdirectory(app)
 
-qt_add_translations(app
-    TS_FILES
-        ${ts_files}
-    SOURCES
-        app/qml/qml.qrc
-)
+if(TARGET Qt6::lrelease)
+    qt_add_translations(app
+        TS_FILES
+            ${ts_files}
+        SOURCES
+            app/qml/qml.qrc
+    )
+endif()
 
 if(ENABLE_TESTING)
     enable_testing()
@@ -46,5 +48,7 @@
     add_subdirectory(tests)
 endif()
 
-set_property(DIRECTORY tests PROPERTY QT_EXCLUDE_FROM_TRANSLATION ON)
+if(ENABLE_TESTING)
+    set_property(DIRECTORY tests PROPERTY QT_EXCLUDE_FROM_TRANSLATION ON)
+endif()
 
--- a/lib/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/lib/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -254,8 +254,13 @@
     CXX_STANDARD_REQUIRED TRUE
 )
 
